# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SECURITY HEADERS, AND THE ONE THAT IS A PROMISE (2026-09-09).
#
# This file had caching and nothing else. What follows is ordinary hardening
# for a public page plus one line that is not ordinary at all:
# `connect-src`.
#
# **"Nothing leaves your phone" is a claim this game makes in prose** —
# `meta/report.ts`'s privacy contract, the manual, and the reason the fonts are
# self-hosted at all (Ashwake 1 fell into a CDN on 2026-08-20 and climbed out).
# A claim in prose is a claim a reader has to take on trust. `connect-src`
# makes the browser enforce it: this app may talk to its own origin and to
# Sentry, and to nothing else, ever, whatever a future bundle happens to
# contain. The Sentry host is there because ONE outbound request exists and it
# is consented — a crash report leaves only when a human taps SEND REPORT, on
# the failure panel or in SETTINGS ▸ LAST ERROR (`shell/failure.ts`).
#
# **`blob:` IS IN `script-src`, AND IT HAS TO BE.** This is the one directive
# here that was got wrong first and measured second.
#
# `troika-three-text` — the board's label renderer — starts its glyph worker
# from a blob URL, and then that worker calls `importScripts` on ANOTHER blob
# URL to rehydrate its module. A worker inherits the document's policy, and
# `importScripts` inside it is governed by `script-src`, not by `worker-src`.
# So `worker-src 'self' blob:` alone let the worker start and then killed it
# from the inside: *"worker module init function failed to rehydrate"*, six
# times, and a board with **no numbers and no marks on it at all**.
#
# That is the exact failure `e2e/helpers.ts` documents for Playwright's WebKit,
# where the same refusal is a harness artifact. Shipping this policy without
# `blob:` would have made it real, in every browser, on the deployed build only
# — `vite preview` serves no `_headers`, so nothing before a deploy would have
# said a word. `e2e/csp.spec.ts` runs the game under this exact policy, read
# from this exact file, which is how it was found before it shipped.
#
# The cost is named: `blob:` in `script-src` means a script this page GENERATES
# may run. On a page with no user input, no cookies, no session and no
# server-rendered anything, that is a far smaller surface than the external
# scripts this still bars — and the alternative is a game whose board cannot
# print a number.
#
# **`script-src` AND `style-src` CARRY HASHES, AND THE BUILD WRITES THEM
# (2026-09-10, `PASS.md` P8.4).** This block used to say `'unsafe-inline'` and
# confess to it: the page runs one inline classic script — the browser floor
# guard, which must parse on engines the module bundle cannot — and one inline
# `<style>`, the pre-JS paint, "both static, so both could be hashed; the
# hashes would have to be computed at build time and written here, which is a
# build step this repository does not have yet."
#
# It has one now. `vite.config.ts`'s `contentPolicy` plugin reads the BUILT
# `dist/index.html`, hashes every inline block in it, and substitutes the two
# marks below on the way out; the file in `public/` is the source and the file
# in `dist/` is what the edge serves. It throws if a mark is missing, if the
# built page has no inline block of a kind, or if `'unsafe-inline'` survives
# anywhere — because a browser handed a hash IGNORES `'unsafe-inline'`, so the
# two together are a policy that reads hardened and enforces nothing.
#
# Why this directive was worth a build step: `'unsafe-inline'` in `script-src`
# means any inline `<script>` that reaches this document runs, which is the
# whole mechanism the directive exists to stop — with it there, the rest of the
# policy is decorative. `e2e/csp.spec.ts` now injects one and asserts it does
# not run, under the generated policy, in a real browser.
#
# And `style-src` cost two edits to `index.html`, which is the part worth
# knowing: **a hash covers the TEXT of a block and never a `style` attribute.**
# The floor guard wrote its sentence with inline styles and so did the
# `<noscript>`, so both moved into the hashed `<style>` as `.floor` — otherwise
# `style-src` would have needed `'unsafe-inline'` (or `'unsafe-hashes'`, which
# is barely narrower) no matter how many hashes it carried. Nothing in
# `apps/game/src` writes a style attribute or a `<style>`: React sets styles
# through the CSSOM, which no CSP governs.
#
# `frame-ancestors` and `X-Frame-Options` together: nobody frames this game,
# and the second is for engines that never learned the first.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'none'; script-src 'self' __INLINE_SCRIPT_HASHES__ blob:; style-src 'self' __INLINE_STYLE_HASHES__; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self'; worker-src 'self' blob:; child-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self' https://o4510241708244992.ingest.us.sentry.io; manifest-src 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# The fingerprinted bundle is immutable by construction — a new build asks
# for different names — so a returning visitor should never pay sixteen
# conditional round trips re-validating it (2026-08-20, launch audit; the
# platform default is max-age=0 must-revalidate on everything). index.html,
# version.json and the worker itself keep the default: they are the files
# whose freshness IS the deploy.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
